rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"0dcded33b772853d6a59dbf2b4672e62f177f12f9ddf22b071756e204269b3fd","event_uuid":"cea37944-b829-4602-8634-7fd684f46cf1","position":{"commit_sha":"5fd80937d9ef0c29b6dfc2dc6d546fc04a2d7a27","position":"1793415911619155990-cea37944-b829-4602-8634-7fd684f46cf1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Cite re-verification against origin/main 360d504f5ceb (2026-09-07). Every `path:line` cite in the description was checked against the attested tip: none had drifted (the description was already re-based on 4c77d6f3e96f, and no cited file changed between 4c77d6f3e96f and 360d504f5ceb). Only the basis sentence changed (4c77d6f3e96f -> 360d504f5ceb). Note: the recorded file_impact reasons still carry the older cites `manifest.py :302-303` and `attest_gate.py :149,:193`; on the tip those constructs are at `manifest.py:321-322` and `attest_gate.py:159,:203` as the description already says. `_uncertified_plan_review_reason` is at `attest_gate.py:99-112` and the `\"verdict\": result.get(...)` passthrough at `:159`, both as cited.","timestamp":1788838422614284001},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Plan amended: `key_not_valid_at_era` is NOT reachable from `plan_review_status`\n\nThe original defect-5 analysis called the enum \"misaligned in BOTH directions\" and step 5 / AC3 required *adding* `key_not_valid_at_era`. Direct measurement disproves the reachability claim, so the description has been amended to a one-directional correction: drop `not-closed`, add nothing.\n\n**What was measured** (worktree `impl-a018`, tree at `origin/main` + this change):\n\n1. **The plan's supporting citation names a file with zero occurrences.** The description cited `tests/unit/test_opcert_cross_environment_c21f.py:225` as observing the leak. `grep -c \"key_not_valid_at_era\"` on that file returns **0**. The cite has been removed.\n\n2. **Every producer of the literal in `src/`** is `attest/opcert.py:308` and `:330`, both inside `verify_opcert`. The remaining hits are docstrings (`authorship.py:324`, `trusted_env.py:169`, `opcert.py:207`), the `verify_signature_result` schema, `types.py:384`, and consumers (`_engine_support/validate.py:121`, `_commands/verify_authorship.py`).\n\n3. **`verify_opcert` has exactly one `src` caller:** `attest/trusted_env.py:181`, inside `verify_required_environment`, reached only from `_commands/verify_opcert.py` — the `rebar verify-opcert` merge gate.\n\n4. **The `plan_review_status` path never reaches it.** The chain is `attest_gate.py:145` → `signing.verify_signature:267` → `signing.verify_attestation_record:128` → `_opcert_verify.verify_opcert_record:163` → `registry.verify` → `scheme.verify`. `_opcert_verify.py` computes its verdict solely from `registry.verify(OPCERT_KIND, envelope, trust_root)`; it imports `authorship` only for `allowed_signers_from_keys` (`:158`, `:267`), never for a verdict. `attest/registry.py` contains **0** occurrences of the literal.\n\nDeclaring `key_not_valid_at_era` on this surface would therefore have documented a value the gate cannot produce — the same class of defect as the `not-closed` member the story exists to remove.\n\n**What changed in the description:** defect 5's analysis, approach step 5, approach step 7 (release-note scope), the `test_mcp_plan_review_status.py` test-plan bullet (7 verdicts → 6), and AC3. AC3 is now:\n\n```\n{'not-closed','key_not_valid_at_era'}.isdisjoint(e), {'mismatch','invalid','foreign_key','unavailable','unknown_kind','unknown_scheme'} <= e\n```\n\nwhich prints `True True` against the implemented schema — it now pins the absence of **both** unreachable verdicts rather than asserting one of them belongs.\n\n**The implementation already matched the measurement** and needed no change: the schema drops `not-closed` and adds nothing; the \"last 6 values\" clause remains accurate; the new test parametrizes over the 6 reachable verdicts and carries a parametrized *negative* case asserting the schema rejects both `not-closed` and `key_not_valid_at_era`. `docs/release-notes.md` already recorded the exclusion and its reasoning. The amendment brings the plan up to the implementation, not the reverse.\n\nDescription trimmed from 8,795 to 7,966 chars to stay under the 8,000 plan-review admission cap.\n","timestamp":1793410037476821707}],"created_at":1788805475236486029,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nFive residues in the plan-review attestation stack, each confirmed by semantic reference search and string grep. Cites re-measured on origin/main `38f8587f65d`.\n\n**1. Dead kwarg.** `manifest.py:289 _hash_basis(repo_root=None, *, at_current_gate_ref=False)`. No src caller passes it (all 5 call sites are under `src/rebar/llm/`: `code_review/region_gate.py:62`, `code_review/sidecar.py:258`, `plan_review/attest.py:226`, `manifest.py:440`, `workflow/plan_review_recovery.py:193`). Its branch `:302-303` delegates to `gate_ref_hash_basis` (`manifest.py:240`), which is independently reachable and stays. Only `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_ref_coherence.py:171,176,181,218` pass it. `docs/adr/0002-code-drift-invalidation.md:119` records the signature.\n\n**2. Unconsumed function.** `read_set.py:189-214 terraform_membership_entries`, plus its comment/constant `:185-186 _TERRAFORM_GLOB_SUFFIXES` — no src caller; only `tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_plan_review_tools.py:223-231`. ADR 0115 `:86-87` defers remote module *content*, not membership globs, so nothing awaits it; under ADR 0111 code waiting for a consumer is deleted.\n\n**3. Behaviourless enum member.** `pin_health.py:15 PlanValidityProfile` is read in exactly one place, `attest.py:665 if profile is PlanValidityProfile.DEFAULT`, so `CLOSE` and `DRIFT_REFRESH` (`pin_health.py:18`) are identical; nothing serialises `.value`/`.name`. `test_attestation_invalidation.py:262-291` exists only to assert that equivalence.\n\n**4. Duplicated message.** `attest.py:426` and `:466` render a byte-identical \"… could not be resolved to a snapshot …\" from two arms.\n\n**5. Status enum declares a value the surface cannot emit.** `src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_status.schema.json:11` declares `not-closed`, which `compute_validity` emits only under `kind == \"completion-verifier\"` (`attest.py:622-628`); `test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py:23,54` already asserts its exclusion from that vocabulary. `attest_gate.py:159` passes `verify_signature`'s verdict through verbatim, and the 6 signature-check verdicts it can carry are declared deliberately. `key_not_valid_at_era` is **not** a 7th member and must NOT be added: its only producers are `attest/opcert.py:308,330` inside `verify_opcert`, whose sole `src` caller is `attest/trusted_env.py:181`, reached only from `_commands/verify_opcert.py` (the `rebar verify-opcert` merge gate). The status path runs `attest_gate.py:145` → `signing.verify_attestation_record:128` → `_opcert_verify.verify_opcert_record` → `registry.verify`, which never reaches `verify_opcert`; `attest/registry.py` contains no occurrence of the literal. The pass-through is contract — `test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py:63,65` assert these verdicts bucket as `infra` (fail-open). The correction is one-directional: drop `not-closed`, add nothing. Neither `_mcp_models.py` nor `types.py` mirrors `PlanReviewStatus`, so the schema is the sole declaration.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. **`manifest.py`** — delete the `:302-303` branch and the kwarg's docstring text (`:294` plus the mode bullet); signature becomes `def _hash_basis(repo_root=None) -> str`. Strip the kwarg's name from `gate_ref_hash_basis`'s docstring at `:244`.\n2. **`read_set.py`** — delete `:185-186` and `:189-214`.\n3. **`pin_health.py`** — delete `DRIFT_REFRESH` (`:18`). `attest.py:244` becomes `profile=PlanValidityProfile.CLOSE` with the comment \"CLOSE = skip code-freshness (the only non-DEFAULT behaviour)\"; reword the `attest.py:534` comment naming `DEFAULT/DRIFT_REFRESH`. Unchanged (all name DEFAULT or CLOSE): `_commands/gates.py:229`, `attest_gate.py:172`, `code_review/bugfix_size_gate.py:232`, `docs/plan-review-gate.md:1099`. `attest.drift_refresh_candidate` keeps its name — only the member it passes changes.\n4. **`attest.py`** — add `_unresolvable_ref_reason(ref: str | None) -> str` (`named = f\"'{ref}'\" if ref else \"the configured gate ref\"`); `:426` and `:466` each return it.\n5. **Align the enum, leaving the `attest_gate.py:159` pass-through UNCHANGED** — in the schema `:11` drop `not-closed`; add nothing (see defect 5). The enum description's \"The last 6 values (…)\" clause already names exactly the 6 reachable verdicts and stays as-is. Mirror the drop in `attest_gate.py:203` and `_mcp_reads.py:37`. `llm/gate_runs.py:379` is the completion-verifier surface where `not-closed` IS reachable — leave it.\n6. **`docs/adr/0002-code-drift-invalidation.md:119`** — amend the recorded signature to `_hash_basis(repo_root)` and append an amendment note in the file's existing \"*(amended by …)*\" style, naming this story and pointing the gate-ref mode at `gate_ref_hash_basis`. It must not retain the kwarg's name; AC1 greps `docs`.\n7. **`docs/release-notes.md`** — one entry: the enum is realigned with what the surface emits (`not-closed` out, nothing added); backward-compatible under `docs/api-stability.md:23`. The entry also records why `key_not_valid_at_era` is deliberately NOT declared here, so a later reader does not re-propose it.\n\n## Scope\n\nOut of scope: `_legacy_material_ok` (`attest.py:727`, callers `:71,634,687`, corpus contract `llm/evals/plan_replay/corpus.py:10,39`); the delta explainers; `compute_validity`'s completion arm. Two fixtures (`cloud_adf_corpus/bodies_00.json`, `dc_wiki_corpus/code_arrow.json`) quote `at_current_gate_ref` inside frozen report bodies — immutable corpus data, which is why AC1 carries `':!tests/fixtures'`.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `test_ref_coherence.py:171,176,181,218` → `manifest.gate_ref_hash_basis(str(repo)).path`; assertions unchanged. Reword the comments at `:167,174,178` that name the kwarg (AC1 greps `tests`).\n- Delete `test_terraform_plan_review_tools.py:223-231`.\n- `test_attestation_invalidation.py:262-291` asserts `close[\"valid\"] is refresh[\"valid\"] is True` and `close[\"health\"] == refresh[\"health\"]` — a pure CLOSE/DRIFT_REFRESH equivalence test. Swapping the member would leave it comparing a value to itself, so **delete the `refresh` block and both equivalence assertions**, keeping the `default`/`close` arms and asserting `default[\"verdict\"] == \"stale-head\"` and `close[\"valid\"] is True`.\n- `.DRIFT_REFRESH` → `.CLOSE` at `test_plan_review_phase_validity.py:35`, `test_plan_material_pin_health_heldout.py:106`, `test_drift_refresh_candidate.py:56`.\n- New `test_plan_review_attest_drift.py::test_unresolvable_ref_reason_is_single_sourced`: the scoped and unscoped paths both yield `_unresolvable_ref_reason(ref)` verbatim.\n- New parametrized test in `test_mcp_plan_review_status.py` over the 6 `verify_signature` failure verdicts this surface can emit: each passes through unchanged as `verdict` and validates against the schema via `jsonschema`; plus a parametrized negative case asserting the schema now REJECTS both unreachable verdicts, `not-closed` and `key_not_valid_at_era`.\n- Unchanged: `test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py` (whole file), `test_compute_validity.py:28`, `plan_review/test_94a3_material_diff.py:428`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `git grep -n \"at_current_gate_ref\\|terraform_membership_entries\\|DRIFT_REFRESH\\|_TERRAFORM_GLOB_SUFFIXES\" -- src tests docs ':!tests/fixtures'` prints nothing.\n- [ ] `git grep -c \"could not be resolved to a snapshot\" -- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py` prints `1`.\n- [ ] `python -c \"import json;e=set(json.load(open('src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_status.schema.json'))['properties']['verdict']['enum']);print({'not-closed','key_not_valid_at_era'}.isdisjoint(e), {'mismatch','invalid','foreign_key','unavailable','unknown_kind','unknown_scheme'} <= e)\"` prints `True True`.\n- [ ] `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest_gate.py` still contains `\"verdict\": result.get(\"verdict\", \"unsigned\"),` — the pass-through is retained, not suppressed.\n- [ ] `grep -c \"not-closed\" src/rebar/llm/gate_runs.py` prints `1`.\n- [ ] Both new tests are green, and `tests/unit/test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py` passes **unmodified**.\n- [ ] `python -m rebar.schemas.gen_types --check` is clean; `make verify` exits 0.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/manifest.py","reason":"delete :302-303 branch, kwarg docstring :244,:294, signature :289"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/read_set.py","reason":"delete :185-186 and :189-214"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pin_health.py","reason":"drop DRIFT_REFRESH :18"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py","reason":":244 CLOSE, :534 comment, :426/:466 via new _unresolvable_ref_reason"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest_gate.py","reason":"docstring :203 drop not-closed, :208 add key_not_valid_at_era; :159 unchanged"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py","reason":"docstring :37 drop not-closed, :40 add key_not_valid_at_era"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_status.schema.json","reason":":11 enum and its description sentence"},{"path":"docs/adr/0002-code-drift-invalidation.md","reason":":119 amend signature + amendment note"},{"path":"docs/release-notes.md","reason":"one entry"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_ref_coherence.py","reason":":171,176,181,218 calls; :167,174,178 comments"},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_plan_review_tools.py","reason":"delete :223-231"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_attestation_invalidation.py","reason":":262-291 drop refresh block and equivalence assertions"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_plan_review_phase_validity.py","reason":":35 DRIFT_REFRESH -> CLOSE"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_plan_material_pin_health_heldout.py","reason":":106 DRIFT_REFRESH -> CLOSE"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_drift_refresh_candidate.py","reason":":56 DRIFT_REFRESH -> CLOSE"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_plan_review_attest_drift.py","reason":"new test_unresolvable_ref_reason_is_single_sourced"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_mcp_plan_review_status.py","reason":"new parametrized 7-verdict pass-through + schema validation test"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["parent","87d8-8bb6-5226-4a5b"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"87d8-8bb6-5226-4a5b","parent_status_uuid":"f3dec7d6-f6b0-4237-9bee-bcfe526c057f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["complexity-reduction","breaking-pass-4"],"ticket_id":"a018-a2c0-fc15-434c","ticket_type":"story","title":"Plan-review attestation: delete confirmed-dead helpers, fold the duplicated ref message, align the status enum with the wire","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["397d2807-7d33-4160-a8be-dafda0232c34","1eb278db-06ec-445e-b7fd-19ab7961714d","f4ae836a-c1cd-4f8b-9fa4-f593d29c3d5f","8963eb97-b8a8-41a4-a0c9-96398cec2379","ab3195f1-7a06-40f3-9797-a2432610f5a3","231e1282-081a-4f65-8ba4-cb1ab4a016d8","1a5a16f6-6605-48cd-a3e9-1d0f2039d7d8","f3dec7d6-f6b0-4237-9bee-bcfe526c057f","02e51b66-43ff-4738-9b9c-b7c4d0e77d14","7daf4eb0-9370-49c7-bb46-a251cd16bd03","54525d2e-751e-406d-9868-b49754b